experiment: axisjit
  the question      §41 run 2c. axisear v2 measured that f3 costs F1 11.3%
                    of its d'. WHY? Level, spectral masking, or the f3
                    JITTER becoming audible and inflating every other
                    axis's denominator?
  the manipulation  hold an axis EXACTLY at rest instead of jittering it,
                    drawing and discarding its deviate so the RNG stream
                    and every other parameter are untouched.
  the built-in null the same freeze at render_f3_gain 0, where f3 is
                    inaudible and freezing it MUST do nothing. A freeze
                    that moves THAT column is a leak, and voids the run.
  the ruler         as axisear v2: signed d'^2 from `cepstral_dprime`,
                    unbiased, the root taken once after averaging reps.

  render_f3_gain 0   <- THE SHIPPED CREATURE
