  CLAUSE 1 -- THE NULL: at render_f3_gain 0 the third resonator does not
  exist, so freezing f3's jitter cannot be heard and must not move any
  axis by more than 2.447 x its paired SE. A freeze that moves this column
  is reaching something it should not, and nothing below is readable.
    f0    dd'^2   0.0000 +- 0.0000   -> flat, as it must be
    f1    dd'^2   0.0000 +- 0.0000   -> flat, as it must be
    f2    dd'^2   0.0000 +- 0.0000   -> flat, as it must be
    bw1   dd'^2   0.0000 +- 0.0000   -> flat, as it must be
    bw2   dd'^2   0.0000 +- 0.0000   -> flat, as it must be
    bw3   dd'^2   0.0000 +- 0.0000   -> flat, as it must be

  CLAUSE 2 -- THE TEST on F1: how much of f3's cost does freezing f3's
  jitter give back? Both ends are measured, so the branches are written
  against their own SEs and not against a midpoint I chose.
    the cost       gain 0 -> gain 1, nothing frozen   dd'^2  -10.127 +-  0.324
    the recovery   at gain 1, freeze f3's jitter      dd'^2    2.934 +-  0.154
    recovered fraction of the cost                       0.290

  CLAUSE 3 -- THE SHAPE: jitter inflation predicts the freeze helps EVERY
  axis at gain 1, because an inflated denominator is shared. Masking
  predicts it helps the spectrally adjacent ones most.
    f0    freezing f3 at gain 1:  dd'^2    2.421 +-  0.336   -> HELPS
    f1    freezing f3 at gain 1:  dd'^2    2.934 +-  0.154   -> HELPS
    f2    freezing f3 at gain 1:  dd'^2    5.980 +-  0.360   -> HELPS
    bw1   freezing f3 at gain 1:  dd'^2    0.005 +-  0.005   -> flat
    bw2   freezing f3 at gain 1:  dd'^2   -0.003 +-  0.008   -> flat
    bw3   freezing f3 at gain 1:  dd'^2    0.007 +-  0.006   -> flat

  AND THE WHOLE OFF-AXIS JITTER BURDEN, same mechanism at full size:
    F1 at gain 0, freezing ALL off-axis jitter:  dd'^2  178.468 +-  4.577
    F1 at gain 1, freezing ALL off-axis jitter:  dd'^2  201.770 +-  5.127

  BOTH, AND THE SPLIT IS THE RESULT. The freeze gives back 0.290 of f3's
  cost -- resolvably more than nothing and resolvably less than all of
  it. So the creature's audible jitter on f3 carries part of the tax and
  the static third formant carries the rest, and neither candidate alone
  accounts for it.
